[Intro]

[Verse 1]
[01:10.08]The first snow fell on the cairn we made
[01:14.33]The second on the door we shut
[01:18.18]The third upon the empty hearth
[01:21.75]And the fourth upon the fourth, and so on

[01:26.59]We counted moons until we could not
[01:29.72]We counted hens until we ate the last
[01:33.95]We counted children by their breathing
[01:37.37]And then we counted them by their stillness

[Pre-Chorus]
[01:42.29]Hvar er sól? Hvar er vár?
[01:45.47]Where is the sun? Where is the spring?

[Chorus]
[01:49.68]This is the winter that forgot its end!
[01:53.46]This is the year that did not turn!
[01:57.24]The gods have sheathed the summer sword!
[02:00.81]The fires we lit shall no more burn!
[02:04.91]Fimbulvetr! Án vár! Án sól!
[02:08.49]The wolves walk bold upon the road!
[02:12.31]The white doth eat the world entire
[02:15.87]And the world hath nothing left it owed!

[Verse 2]
[02:35.58]The priests did pray to the gilt new god
[02:39.47]The vǫlur did sing to the old
[02:43.27]The smith did beat his iron warm
[02:46.82]But the iron grew cold, and cold, and cold

[02:51.12]The young ones asked what summer was
[02:54.77]And we could not remember well
[02:58.66]We told them of a yellow light
[03:02.08]That fell on grass — but they could not tell

[Pre-Chorus]
[03:07.46]Hvar er sól? Hvar er vár?
[03:10.56]Where is the sun? Where is the spring?

[Chorus]
[03:14.95]This is the winter that forgot its end!
[03:18.30]This is the year that did not turn!
[03:22.17]The gods have sheathed the summer sword!
[03:25.82]The fires we lit shall no more burn!
[03:29.91]Fimbulvetr! Án vár! Án sól!
[03:33.69]The wolves walk bold upon the road!
[03:37.45]The white doth eat the world entire
[03:41.01]And the world hath nothing left it owed!

[Bridge]
[03:49.26]We called upon the forest-mother
[03:56.87]We called as we had called before
[04:04.74]But the wood was buried under snow
[04:12.17]And the wood did answer us no more

[04:20.78]Heyr oss, Skogarmóðir
[04:24.46]Heyr oss... heyr oss...
[04:28.41]She doth not heareth
[04:31.90]She doth not heareth us now

[Breakdown]
[04:44.44]The hearth! Is cold!
[04:47.54]The horn! Is dry!
[04:51.39]The crow! Hath frozen! In the sky!

[Final Chorus]
[05:11.46]This is the winter that forgot its end!
[05:15.13]This is the year that did not turn!
[05:19.09]The gods have sheathed the summer sword!
[05:22.53]The fires we lit shall no more burn!
[05:26.73]Fimbulvetr! Án vár! Án sól!
[05:30.31]The wolves walk bold upon the road!
[05:34.20]The white doth eat the world entire
[05:37.85]And the world hath nothing left it owed!

[Outro]
[05:48.96]Hvar er vár...?
